                 cause in children and adults overall, although N meningitidis
                 causes most disease in patients between ages 2 and 18 years.
                 Broad-spectrum cephalosporins (eg, ceftriaxone, cefotaxime) are
                 considered the agents of choice for empirical treatment of
                 bacterial meningitis. However, use of these agents will have to
                 be reconsidered if the incidence of invasive infection from
                 drug-resistant S pneumoniae continues to increase. The role of
